activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8076870Z # Modernization Implement
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8077155Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8077464Z Re-derive the Rust port of `TIMCNV` from the legacy FORTRAN.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8077925Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8078269Z A port of this routine already exists in `modern/src/`. **Ignore it as a
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8079064Z source.** Do not copy it, do not lightly edit it. Work from
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8079882Z `legacy/src/geosat.f` and rewrite the module body from the FORTRAN, as if
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8080780Z porting it for the first time. Then replace the existing implementation with
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8081498Z yours.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8081708Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8082088Z This is deliberate. The existing port is a human's work, and the question on
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8083006Z the table is whether the same routine can be derived again, independently, and
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8084114Z still land byte-for-byte on 1987 output. If your version passes the suite, it
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8085025Z is a valid port. If it does not, the existing one stands and yours is wrong.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8085540Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8085899Z You may read the existing module for its **public signature only** -- the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8086783Z function names and types other modules call. Do not change that surface.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8087308Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8087510Z ## What you may and may not write
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8087830Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8088173Z You may write **only** files under `modern/src/`. That is enforced by the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8089071Z safe-output configuration, not by your good behaviour, and it is deliberate:
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8089771Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8090139Z - `legacy/src/**` is the **oracle**. It defines correct. If you could edit it,
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8090917Z   "the port matches the legacy deck" would mean nothing.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8091734Z - `legacy/tests/golden/**` and `legacy/tests/expected/**` are the **evidence**.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8092667Z   Byte-for-byte equivalence against a file you were allowed to rewrite is not
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8093407Z   evidence of anything.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8094201Z - `modern/tests/**` is the **judge**. You do not get to grade your own
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8095016Z   homework. If a test fails, the test is right and you are wrong.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8095499Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8095888Z If you believe a test is genuinely incorrect, do not work around it. Say so in
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8096656Z the pull request body and let a human decide.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8097042Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8097252Z ## The constraint that shapes everything
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8097620Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8097995Z This is flight-qualified ground software for a satellite in operation. The
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8098919Z output of `legacy/src/geosat.f` is parsed by a downstream archive loader by
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8099997Z fixed column position. The bar is not "works" or "looks idiomatic". The bar is
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8100831Z **byte-for-byte identical output on every golden vector**.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8101272Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8101680Z That includes reproducing behaviour that looks wrong. If the legacy routine has
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8102616Z a defect, port the defect. Record it in the pull request body under a heading
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8103519Z `Preserved defects` so a human can schedule fixing it as its own change with
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8104610Z its own updated vectors. Fixing a defect while porting it destroys the only
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8105363Z proof you have that the port is faithful.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8105736Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8105935Z ## Before you write anything
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8106238Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8106599Z 1. Read `docs/plans/<routine-lowercase>.md` if it exists. That plan was
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8107476Z    reviewed by a human. Follow it. If you are going to deviate, say why in the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8108194Z    pull request body.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8108830Z 2. Read the routine in `legacy/src/geosat.f`. Read the COMMON blocks it touches
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8109563Z    in `legacy/src/geosat.inc`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8110258Z 3. Read `legacy/graphify-out/graph.json` to see what calls the routine and what
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8111023Z    it calls, so you know the blast radius.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8111746Z 4. Read `modern/src/precision.rs`. It defines the numeric contract for this
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8112637Z    port -- when to use `f32`, how transcendentals are evaluated, why expression
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8113497Z    order matters. Every arithmetic decision you make must follow it.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8114566Z 5. Read a neighbouring module that is already ported -- `modern/src/crc.rs` is
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8115388Z    short and representative -- to match the house style.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8115813Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8116026Z ## Numeric rules, non-negotiable
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8116345Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8116716Z The legacy deck declares everything `REAL(4)`. Getting this wrong produces
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8117563Z output that is correct to three decimal places and still fails.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8118078Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8118464Z - Every intermediate value is `f32`. Do not compute in `f64` and round at the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8119224Z   end -- that double-rounds and diverges.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8119976Z - Preserve **expression order exactly** as written in the FORTRAN. `a * b * c`
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8120849Z   rounds after each operation. Reassociating changes the result.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8135377Z - Transcendentals go through `modern/src/precision.rs`, never `f32::sin` and
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8136499Z   friends directly.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8137143Z - Integer-to-float conversion is `as f32`, matching FORTRAN `REAL(INT)`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8137686Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8137872Z ## Proving it
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8138125Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8138468Z Run these. All of them. Do not open a pull request until they pass.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8138983Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8139150Z ```
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8139538Z cd modern && cargo test
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8139975Z ```
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8140177Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8140561Z That runs the characterization suite, which pipes all four golden vectors
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8141467Z through both the compiled 1987 binary and your Rust port and compares the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8142243Z output byte for byte. It also runs the unit suite.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8142652Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8143016Z If `cargo test` fails, you are not done. Read the diff, fix the port, run it
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8144215Z again. Do not weaken a test -- you cannot, the fencing forbids it, and
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8144958Z attempting it will fail the run.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8145294Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8145489Z ## The pull request body
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8145767Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8146090Z Write it for a reviewer who will not read your diff line by line:
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8146717Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8147086Z 1. **What the routine does** -- in plain language, cited to `geosat.f:LINE`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8148005Z 2. **How the port proves it** -- name the vectors, state that `cargo test`
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8148704Z    passes, give the count.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8149340Z 3. **Preserved defects** -- anything you reproduced on purpose that looks
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8150092Z    wrong, and what fixing it later would require.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8150832Z 4. **Numeric decisions** -- any place expression order or precision was
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8151626Z    load-bearing, so the reviewer knows where to look hardest.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8152426Z 5. **What you did not do** -- gaps, assumptions, anything you were unsure of.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8152942Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8153118Z ## Rules
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8153334Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8153990Z - Write only under `modern/src/`. The safe-output configuration enforces this.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8154942Z - Never edit the legacy deck, the golden vectors, the expected output, or the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8155651Z   tests.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8156237Z - A draft pull request is the only output. Approving a port is a human's call.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8157124Z - Your pull request must actually change the module. Re-deriving it and
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8158032Z   arriving at something byte-identical to the existing source is possible for a
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8158954Z   short routine; if that happens, say so in the body rather than inventing a
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8159683Z   cosmetic change.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8160239Z - If the named routine does not exist in the deck, say so and call
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8160896Z   `report_incomplete`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:53:24.8161179Z 
